        {
          "title": "Same Patient, Different Order: Action-Level Reliability of Clinical LLM Agents Under Repeated Runs",
          "title_zh": "同一患者，不同医嘱：重复运行下临床 LLM 智能体的动作级可靠性",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2609.13582v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.13582",
          "summary": "The authors introduce a \"same-input rerun\" protocol that replays a task with every input held fixed and compares the resulting orders rather than the score, and apply it to 1000 MedAgentBench runs across 50 tasks with two quantized open-weight models below ten billion parameters at two temperatures. They find action-level divergence across identical runs that often passes unrecorded by the benchmark score, arguing for repeated-run evaluation and action-level stability reporting.",
