          "title": "FLoKD: Adaptive Knowledge Distillation for Federated Low-Rank LLM over Wireless Networks",
          "title_zh": "FLoKD：无线网络下联邦低秩 LLM 的自适应知识蒸馏",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2609.13580v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.13580",
          "summary": "FLoKD is an adaptive knowledge-distillation framework for federated LoRA fine-tuning of LLMs over wireless networks that communicates intermediate LoRA activations as the distillation signal instead of logits or full parameters. It adds transformer-block importance scoring and two dataset selection strategies, and reports 50-65% lower communication overhead with rapid convergence to competitive perplexity on WikiText-103, PTB and Dialog.",
