          "title": "Mind the Gap: Detecting Description-Execution Mismatch Attacks in DAO Governance",
          "title_zh": "留意差距：检测 DAO 治理中的描述-执行不一致攻击",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2609.13601v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.13601",
          "summary": "The paper presents a framework for detecting Description-Execution Mismatch (DEMI) attacks, in which a DAO proposal's benign-looking natural-language description hides code that transfers funds or seizes control, using a DAO-agnostic simulation that derives execution behavior and an LLM evidence-mapping paradigm that locates per-action textual justifications instead of issuing holistic judgments. On real Ethereum DAO governance data the detector reports 81.7% mean precision and 98.3% mean recall under stratified cross-validation and defends against most adaptive attacks in a red-team/blue-team evaluation.",
