          "title": "AttnFuse: A Composable DSL for Compiling Attentions to Fused GPU Kernels",
          "title_zh": "AttnFuse：将注意力编译为融合 GPU 内核的可组合 DSL",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2609.13612v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.13612",
          "summary": "AttnFuse is a small domain-specific language for attention that makes pre-multiplication transformations such as RoPE first-class operations, letting researchers compose ten building blocks into a variant that compiles to a single fused GPU kernel. It reports a 2.10x speedup over flex_attention on the RoPE+causal pattern on an RTX 3090 and runs a full Llama-3-8B training step within 5% of PyTorch's hand-tuned backend on an H100.",
